{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon","id":336694,"title":"Werewolves on the Moon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-10T21:15:06-08:00","id":336694,"title":"Werewolves on the Moon","content":"I run fairly open-world games, and my players have set it as their goal to reach the moon in person. What consequences and challenges would werewolves, or any of the main splats really, face in their quest to step foot on the body of Mother Luna? Obviously the mortal-related difficulties of engineering another manned lunar mission and talking or sneaking your way onto said mission are to be anticipated - this question is more about what supernatural risks would be incurred in the questing?<br /> <br /> Apologies for any typos / grammatical inconsistencies. It is late and I will attempt to clarify any confusions over the question once I have found some sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T23:09:55-08:00","id":336794,"title":"","content":"The IDIGAM are on the Moon. This is kinda a big deal.<br /> <br /> The local Shadow would be <i>lousy</i> with corrupted spirits of impossible concepts.<br /> <br /> Ironically, most of the complications the Moon might cause due to phases don't happen, because there aren't any phases on the Moon. However, this means that you can't reap the benefits of your Auspice Moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T23:28:03-08:00","id":336799,"title":"","content":"What is interesting is that Kingdom of Mother Goddess of Uratha is <b>filled</b> with monstrous spirits. Should not Luna take care of Idigams herself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T23:40:30-08:00","id":336805,"title":"","content":"She did by imprisoning them up there; otherwise, they'd be Earth's problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T03:55:56-08:00","id":336895,"title":"","content":"Why could she and werewolf just destroy them? Why Luna did not seal the Idigams on HER BODY (Moon's surface)? Just let them free roam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-11-2014, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T05:30:01-08:00","id":336953,"title":"","content":"It's hard to trap the idigam, because they can change form to escape any bindings. So they put them on the moon, which was far enough from Earth that they couldn't get back to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-11-2014, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T06:00:57-08:00","id":336975,"title":"","content":"The Great Predator was unable to destroy the formless idigam, and had to look to Luna for help just to contain them. There's no easy way to keep the idigam on the moon locked away in a box and, besides, there's functionally no difference between that and letting them roam free on the moon's surface - there's nothing there for them to use anyway, until humans come along with a moon lander and everything goes wrong.<br /> <br /> Formless idigam are <i>very</i> hard to kill; Coalesced idigam are more powerful, but at the cost of also being more vulnerable. There's something in the world since the Wolf's death and the sundering of the Gauntlet that pushes idigam to Coalesce; this wasn't the case back in the days of Pangaea, if that myth is true in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T10:04:21-08:00","id":337157,"title":"","content":"Of course, there would also probably be Lunar spirits galore, so you'd have a very high-stakes location, teeming with both the most powerful enemies, and most helpful allies, in the setting. I imagine it would be a bit like the stereotype of a Forgotten Realms game - tons of phenomenally powerful NPCs on both sides, with the PCs just kind of along for the ride while the ST explains all the cool things that are going on outside of their power to influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T10:53:38-08:00","id":337214,"title":"","content":"I'd tend towards overloading the gameplay elements normally connected with the moon. Crazy things like all of their Auspex abilities would be active all the time or Mother Luna gifts have extreme reations. Maybe they gain the Rote quality; maybe each die is an automatic success; or maybe they fail entirely because Luna can't focus on something so close to her.<br /> <br /> Also, combining science with the game, the moon has no shield against the rage of the sun: it gets bombarded with intense radiation all the time. Servants of Helios probably all over the place on the moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T11:30:14-08:00","id":337239,"title":"","content":"So aside from the obvious physical difficulties of getting to the moon, do people thing / is it written anywhere that more occult bans exist to prevent supernatural access to the lunar surface?<br /> <br /> Likewise, according to the GMC, the Archangel of Death was entombed upon the moon until the lunar landings. If I were to add the little bit of crossover it seems that the moon becomes a kind of necropolis-prison for those things too powerful to kill, but too weak to carve their own places in the spiritual hierarchies and survive, with Luna as the warden.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=337157#post337157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, there would also probably be Lunar spirits galore, so you'd have a very high-stakes location, teeming with both the most powerful enemies, and most helpful allies, in the setting. I imagine it would be a bit like the stereotype of a Forgotten Realms game - tons of phenomenally powerful NPCs on both sides, with the PCs just kind of along for the ride while the ST explains all the cool things that are going on outside of their power to influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't this sort of contradict that the Idigam were banished there specifically for the moon's bareness and isolation from all but the most occasional influence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T11:47:09-08:00","id":337280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=336975#post336975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Great Predator was unable to destroy the formless idigam, and had to look to Luna for help just to contain them. There's no easy way to keep the idigam on the moon locked away in a box and, besides, there's functionally no difference between that and letting them roam free on the moon's surface - there's nothing there for them to use anyway, until humans come along with a moon lander and everything goes wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>So no Moon Kingdom of Luna? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://fc06.deviantart.net/fs70/f/2014/159/b/b/the_moon_kingdom_castle__anime__by_moon_shadow_1985-d5lizfj.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T11:52:42-08:00","id":337287,"title":"","content":"Well, what do you think the Dark Kingdom was?<br /> <br /> Also, I never thought about it before, but that shot makes zero sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T12:16:13-08:00","id":337296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=337287#post337287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what do you think the Dark Kingdom was?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prison for Idigams?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=337287#post337287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I never thought about it before, but that shot makes zero sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why it does make zero sense?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T12:37:13-08:00","id":337330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=337296#post337296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why it does make zero sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the moon is in the sky over the moon palace. Which is on the moon if I remember correctly. I've never been clear on the physical placement of locations in that universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T12:56:27-08:00","id":337349,"title":"","content":"Isn't it on the Moon?<br /> <br /> <i>Then how is the Moon in the sky behind it.</i><br /> <br /> Mein gott, we've been lied to! The Supernaturals are hiding a second moon!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T13:00:27-08:00","id":337350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=337349#post337349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it on the Moon?<br /> <br /> <i>Then how is the Moon in the sky behind it.</i><br /> <br /> Mein gott, we've been lied to! The Supernaturals are hiding a second moon!</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's a Vernian twist: the palace is on the inside of the Moon (big &quot;M&quot;) which is actually hallow and contains stars and another moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T1