","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T10:37:49-08:00","id":340123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=339940#post339940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FEAR THE MACHINE AND ITS &quot;ANGELS&quot;. THEY SLIP THROUGH THE CRACKS, AND KILL BEFORE YOU BLINK. DON'T BLINK.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mankind knew not death then. Those whose bodies became worn and aged were sent to sleep in the shadow of the Earth and returned after a time restored to health and youth.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The second Fury was named Death, and fled to the hidden side of the moon. It cursed mankind to forget the way back from the shadow of the Earth.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;As the portal through which death itself entered our universe, it was changed into a thing neither dead nor alive. Those who learn to control it, as its current jailers seek to do, will exert ultimate power over the tides of life and death.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T11:27:29-08:00","id":340148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why did Luna allow the Crypt of the Butterfly which held the Angel of Death to be created on her surface? This is referenced in the opening chapter of the Godmachine Anthology, a copy of the original blue-book fiction that inspired the Godmachine Chronicles. </div> </div> </div>She probably does not care about anything out of the scope of her nature as a Celestine. Nothing related to Spirits, not my problem unless you are suicidal and start poking at her. <br /> <br /> I could maybe even go with such solution that main body of God-Machines resides in Moon's Twilight and Luna would not care as long nothing pestera her in her Shadow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T12:45:36-08:00","id":340177,"title":"","content":"Where is Luna discussed most in-depth? I assume she doesn't have stats, but is there somewhere that more or less describes the spirit and her motivations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T12:50:06-08:00","id":340179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I assume she doesn't have stats, but is there somewhere that more or less describes the spirit and her motivations? </div> </div> </div>I just assume that since it is a Celestine and God-Machine's influence does not overlap with the spirit world there is no room for automatic conflict between the two,<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T13:13:31-08:00","id":340184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=340177#post340177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is Luna discussed most in-depth? I assume she doesn't have stats, but is there somewhere that more or less describes the spirit and her motivations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chapter 1 of Lore of the Forsaken covers a number of her more prominent aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T13:59:44-08:00","id":340210,"title":"","content":"I'm more curious about how Luna would react to her children parking a rocket ship on her face and jumping around like a bouncy house!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T14:04:50-08:00","id":340212,"title":"","content":"^Sounds like teenager phase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T16:16:05-08:00","id":340276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=338349#post338349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of how stupid it probably makes me look, I find myself assuming anything I can't explain through the stuff of any specific splat is Infrastructure. I suspect this may have been intended...</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor derail: I'm not going to say that you sound stupid, and I'm a BIG fan of the God-Machine, but for me that removes a lot of the sheer one-off mysteries that exist in the nWoD, and that kinda makes it all feel a little...small. Well-defined. Organized. I like a measure of messy, undefined space that makes even the most learned occultist blanch at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T20:09:49-08:00","id":340411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=340210#post340210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more curious about how Luna would react to her children parking a rocket ship on her face and jumping around like a bouncy house!</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think she set up the gravity up there the way she did? It's the only way she can get the kids to visit!<br /> <br /> Oh, sure, they are <i>so grateful</i> when your Lunes pull them out of a tight spot, but do they ever write? No, it's all &quot;Mama Luna, can I have some Gifts?&quot; this, or &quot;Mama Luna, why does it burn when I touch silver?&quot; that.<br /> <br /> And don't get me <i>started</i> on those &quot;Pure&quot; brats; they take after their <i>father's</i> side of the family, believe you me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T21:35:55-08:00","id":340490,"title":"","content":"First, could be agree that Luna's Kingdom would be on Light Side of Moon we see every night? And Dark Side is probably the prison for Idigams? And there could be some minor God-Machine Infrastructure, maybe as &quot;embassies&quot; to the court of Luna?<br /> <br /> Second, did not the <b>Apocalypse</b> had a moon bridges, or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T21:41:11-08:00","id":340492,"title":"","content":"Luna's Kingdom is Luna.<br /> <br /> THe problem is that she is literally so large, metaphysically speaking. she can't see some things. If she could, she probably would never have lifted her curses one whit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T21:47:08-08:00","id":340496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=340492#post340492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THe problem is that she is literally so large, metaphysically speaking. she can't see some things. If she could, she probably would never have lifted her curses one whit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting - why you say this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T02:33:26-08:00","id":340672,"title":"","content":"Consider a human and ants. Whenever you are on a walk, do you notice those critters crawling under your feet? You might even step on a one and not notice that at all. Now consider a spiritual embodiment of a Moon compared with few werewolves. The scale is even more disproportionate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T08:25:21-08:00","id":340833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=340672#post340672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider a human and ants. Whenever you are on a walk, do you notice those critters crawling under your feet? You might even step on a one and not notice that at all. Now consider a spiritual embodiment of a Moon compared with few werewolves. The scale is even more disproportionate.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to borrow from Lovecraftian elements: pity poor the ant that <i>does</i> get focused on. Pulled off the ground to run across the fingers of a being beyond it's understanding before, maybe, being put down again. What if actually going to the moon makes you into that special ant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T08:30:25-08:00","id":340838,"title":"","content":"Here's something worrying for you to think about.<br /> <br /> The moon's spiritscape is barren; it's this lack of Essence and spirits that has allowed the idigam to be caged there. Exactly why the moon's Shadow is like that, well, there could be various explanations; the raw power of Luna itself simply hoovers up all the Essence, or it's part of the Warden Moon's nature as a boundary god warding against the alien Shadow beyond its orbit, or the raw cold of the Shadow-void just sucks all it all away. Regardless, the concerning part is that even if you got to the moon, you're not very likely to encounter an idigam.<br /> <br /> Why's that concerning?<br /> <br /> Well, because it tells you that most of the idigam <i>have already escaped</i>.<br /> <br /> And the ones that are left still? The ones that have yet to get out of their lifeless prison?<br /> <br /> Oh, they're berserk with desperation and anticipation, so close to freedom they can <i>taste</i> it, yet terrified that soon the Lunes will perfect some new prison to enclose them forever.<br /> <br /> If one of <i>those</i> idigam comes across you while you're on the moon, well... good luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T10:11:37-08:00","id":340914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=340838#post340838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The moon's spiritscape is barren[...]</div> </div> </div> </div>So where do the Lunes hold court, or are they purely terrestrial spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T15:02:52-08:00","id":341254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=340838#post340838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's something worrying for you to think about.<br /> <br /> The moon's spiritscape is barren; it's this lack of Essence and spirits that has allowed the idigam to be caged there. Exactly why the moon's Shadow is like that, well, there could be various explanations; the raw power of Luna itself simply hoovers up all the Essence, or it's part of the Warden Moon's nature as a boundary god warding against the alien Shadow beyond its orbit, or the raw cold of the Shadow-void just sucks all it all away. Regardless, the concerning part is that even if you got to the moon, you're not very likely to encounter an idigam.<br /> <br /> Why's that concerning?<br /> <br /> Well, because it tells you that most of the idigam <i>have already escaped</i>.<br /> <br /> And the ones that are left still? The ones that have yet to get out of their lifeless prison?<br /> <br /> Oh, they're berserk with desperation and anticipation, so close to freedom they can <i>taste</i> it, yet terrified that soon the Lunes will perfect some new prison to enclose them forever.<br /> <br /> If one of <i>those</i> idigam comes across you while you're on the moon, well... good luck.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;That's one small step for man... what giant leap for - OH GOD, WHAT THE FUCK IS THAT!?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> - Radio Silence -","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T16:30:29-08:00","id":341323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=340914#post340914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So where do the Lunes hold court, or are they purely terrestrial spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of the top of my head (and this may be wrong), they tend to hold court where there is moonlight. While it is technically true that some of the illumination, were you to stand on the moon's surface, is bouncing back at you from the ground around you rather than coming directly from the sun, it's not really symbolically what is meant by moonlight. I generally imagine the Lunes holding mad conclaves in the vaults of the sky where air thins to void, then cascading down with the beams of moonlight to menace the Shadow and manipulate Forsaken; or perhaps they flock in the wake of the Warden Moon's passing, helping their god guard against the void. Some probably dance and caper in an orbit around the moon, keeping well out of reach of the hunger of the idigam dwelling below. It's possible the Lunes do sally down to the moon's surface to attempt to construct deeper prisons for the idigam, or to keep count of their protean prisoners (and maybe wound or torment any that seem to have gathered so much as a scrap of Essence, at least before the inmates got riled up at the prospect of actually escaping - like a prison riot down there, now), but this isn't something I put any word count into describing in the Idigam write-up in 2e since, well, it's not exactly going to be game-relevant information for the vast bulk of chronicles.<br /> <br /> Regardless, wherever they are,<i> don't trust Lunes.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T07:55:52-08:00","id":342912,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;That's one small step for man... what giant leap for - OH GOD, WHAT THE FUCK IS THAT!?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> - Radio Silence - </div> </div> </div>Then it seems in NWoD Neil and Buzz could have been a badass mofos who just dealt with whatever threathened them and ignored as it had not ever happened. Then those entities never approached later astronauts.<br /> <br /> B A S E D <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T19:03:35-08:00","id":346315,"title":"","content":"Fun fact, the dark side of the moon is a myth. The sun illuminates it, but since only one side of the moon is facing earth, we can't see it.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the Idigam are imprisoned inside a realm that does not exist... Luna is mind fucking them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T10:13:20-08:00","id":347512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the Idigam are imprisoned inside a realm that does not exist... Luna is mind fucking them! </div> </div> </div>They are forced to listen to Pink Floyd's discography, played backwards, and on the loop.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T10:43:58-08:00","id":347523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=342912#post342912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Then it seems in NWoD Neil and Buzz could have been a badass mofos who just dealt with whatever threathened them and ignored as it had not ever happened. Then those entities never approached later astronauts.<br /> <br /> B A S E D</div> </div> </div> </div>They never even noticed the idigam consuming the spirits that they'd brought up with them, nor the ancient horrors latching onto the spacecraft to be taken back to Earth. And yes, every other mission to the moon brought back even more Moon-Banished - why materialise and attack the humans who are your ticket out of prison?<br /> <br /> ...either that, or Buzz and Neil were actually Bale Hounds who went up there on purpose for a meet-and-greet with the blasphemous proteans imprisoned by the Warden Moon and offer them a free bus ride back down. All those moon landing photos really are faked, cos the <i>actual</i> photography features Gigeresque amphitheatres of mind-breaking shoggoth-things and warped void-monsters gathered in a congregation, rapt at the preaching of two shapes of twisted flesh and fur laden down with fetishes that kept back the lung-searing emptiness from choking them. There's even a selfie of Buzz doing a V-sign and grinning in Dalu, his other arm round the flowing spirit-substance of Gurdilag (who always looks terrible in photos and manages to look stupid even despite being an eldritch entity from the beginning of time).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T19:58:39-08:00","id":348731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/336694-werewolves-on-the-moon?p=346315#post346315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact, the dark side of the moon is a myth. The sun illuminates it, but since only one side of the moon is facing earth, we can't see it.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the Idigam are imprisoned inside a realm that does not exist... Luna is mind fucking them!</div> </div> </div> </div> What better place for the patron goddess of shapeshifting and insanity to use as a prison than some place that doesn't exist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T08:46:27-08:00","id":350680,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, Werewolves on the Moon sounds like it would be a good song name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T08:49:28-08:00","id":350683,"title":"","content":"^^ It's still my headcanon that Apollo project was partly a collaboration between VALKYRIE and Cheiron to gather samples and send humanity's strongest Hunters to deal with the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date"